## 2. MODULAR ARCHITECTURE OPTIONS
Depending on your exact operational model, your platform will incorporate combinations of the following core modules:

### Module Track A: Media, Content & Community (Culture & Music Focus)
* **Digital Media Engine:** High-performance streaming/playback architecture for audio tracks, video highlights, or podcast-style cultural series.
* **Creator & Contributor Profiles:** Dedicated portals for artists, cultural curators, and content creators to manage submissions and interact with audiences.
* **Community & Social Interaction:** In-app likes, comments, social sharing, and community engagement forums.

### Module Track B: Events, Venues & Fan Engagement (Culture & Sports Focus)
* **Event & Fixture Calendars:** Interactive schedules for upcoming cultural showcases, tours, matches, and sports tournaments.
* **Digital Ticketing & Passes:** In-app ticket booking, dynamic QR code generation for gate entry, and automated receipts.
* **Fan Voting & Polling:** Interactive fan polls, award voting, and match prediction contests.

### Module Track C: Marketplace, Talent & Direct Monetization
* **Talent / Athlete Profiles:** Verified rosters, player statistics, visual portfolios, and scouting inquiry channels.
* **Merchandise & Digital Commerce:** Built-in storefront for cultural merchandise, team kits, digital memorabilia, or creator products.
* **Integrated Payments:** Local and international payment processing (Paystack, cards, bank transfers) for subscriptions, voting credits, or purchases.

### Module Track D: Central Master Admin & Analytics Console
* **Content Moderation & Publishing Desk:** Review, schedule, and approve user-generated or proprietary content across categories.
* **User Management & Role Permissions:** Manage fan tiers, verified creator badges, and administrative staff accounts.
* **Revenue & Traffic Analytics:** Real-time visibility into daily active users (DAU), engagement rates, transactions, and gross platform revenue.

